cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se você usar este software, cite-o com os metadados abaixo. / If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "robocup-vision-pipeline: YOLO detection validated by HSV field segmentation for RoboCup Humanoid Soccer (ROS 2)"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: "de Miranda"
    given-names: "Diego"
  # Outros colaboradores só devem ser listados com o consentimento deles. Em especial, parte do
  # código e dos dados vem do projeto de simulação original (veja "Licença e proveniência" no README).
repository-code: "https://github.com/diegodemiranda/robocup-vision-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/diegodemiranda/robocup-vision-pipeline"
# Reflete o arquivo LICENSE atual. A revisão de licenciamento descrita no README ainda está pendente:
# se a licença mudar, atualize também LICENSE, package.xml e setup.py.
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Vision system for RoboCup humanoid soccer. A YOLO detector (YOLOv8n or YOLO26n) runs alongside a
  classical HSV field segmentation (field boundary, obstacles and line points); a detection is published
  only if it lies inside the segmented field. The segmentation package works on its own, without ROS or a
  detector. Includes a ROS 2 integration, a speed benchmark of YOLOv8n versus YOLO26n and a training and
  evaluation toolkit.
keywords:
  - RoboCup
  - humanoid soccer
  - computer vision
  - object detection
  - YOLO
  - ROS 2
  - HSV segmentation
